<article class="env-example" id="0G3F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G3F">Example <span data-tag="0G3F">15.95.4</span>.</a> Let $p$ be a prime number. Consider the map $\mathbf{Z}_ p[x] \to \mathbf{Z}_ p[y]$ of polynomial algebras sending $x$ to $py$. Consider the cokernel $M = \mathop{\mathrm{Coker}}(\mathbf{Z}_ p[x]^\wedge \to \mathbf{Z}_ p[y]^\wedge )$ of the induced map on (ordinary) $p$-adic completions. Then $M$ is a derived complete $\mathbf{Z}_ p$-module by Proposition <a href="/tag/091T" data-tag="091T">15.93.5</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/091U" data-tag="091U">15.93.6</a>; see also discussion in Example <a href="/tag/09AT" data-tag="09AT">15.95.3</a>. However, $M$ is not $p$-adically complete as $1 + py + p^2 y^2 + \ldots $ maps to a nonzero element of $M$ which is contained in $\bigcap p^ nM$. </p>
</article>